#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:40
msgid ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Print Job Billing and Accounting</b></p>  "
"<p>Insert a meaningful string here to associate the current print job with a "
"certain account. This string will appear in the CUPS \"page_log\" to help with "
"the print accounting in your organization. (Leave it empty if you do not need "
"it.) "
"<p> It is useful for people who print on behalf of different \"customers\", "
"like print service bureaux, letter shops, press and prepress companies, or "
"secretaries who serve different bosses, etc.</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o job-billing=...         # example: \"Marketing_Department\" or "
"\"Joe_Doe\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Druk Taak Rekening en Rekeningkunde</b></p>  "
"<p>Voeg 'n betekenisvolle string hier in om die huidige druk taak  te assosieer "
"met 'n sekere rekening. Hierdie string sal in die CUPS \"bladsy_log\" verskyn "
"om te help met die druk rekeningkunde in jou organisasie. (Los dit oop as jy "
"dit nie nodig het nie). "
"<p> Dit is nuttig vir mense wat namens verskillende \"kliente\" druk soos druk "
"diens buro, briewe winkels, pers en vooraf-pers maatskappye, of sekretaresses "
"wat verskillende base het, bv.</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie afbakening:</em>  "
"<pre>    -taak-rekening=...         # Voorbeeld: \"Bemarking_Departement\" of "
"\"Joe_Doe\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:60
msgid ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Scheduled Printing</b></p>  "
"<p>Scheduled printing lets you control the time of the actual printout, while "
"you can still send away your job <b>now</b> and have it out of your way. "
"<p> Especially useful is the \"Never (hold indefinitely)\" option. It allows "
"you to park your job until a time when you (or a printer administrator) decides "
"to manually release it. "
"<p> This is often required in enterprise environments, where you normally are "
"not allowed to directly and immediately access the huge production printers in "
"your <em>Central Repro Department</em>. However it is okay to send jobs to the "
"queue which is under the control of the operators (who, after all, need to make "
"sure that the 10,000 sheets of pink paper which is required by the Marketing "
"Department for a particular job are available and loaded into the paper "
"trays).</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o job-hold-until=...      # example: \"indefinite\" or \"no-hold\"  "
"</pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Geskeduleerde Druk</b></p>  "
"<p>Geskeduleerde druk laat jou die tyd beheer van die eintlike uitdruk, terwyl "
"jy steeds jou werk <b>nou</b> kan wegstuur  en dit uit jou pad hê. "
"<p>Veral handig is die \"Nooit (hou onbepaald)\" opsie. Dit laat jou toe om jou "
"werk te parkeer tot 'n tyd wanneer jy (of 'n drukker administrateur) besluit om "
"dit handeliks vry te stel.  "
"<p> Hierdie word dikwels vereis in onderneming omgewings, waar jy normaalweg "
"nie toegelaat word om direk en onmiddellik toegang te verkry tot die groot "
"produksie drukkers in jou <em> Sentrale Repro Departement nie</em>"
". In elk geval is dit goed om take na die ry te stuur wat onder die beheer van "
"die operateurs is (wie, na alles, moet seker maak dat die 10,000 velle pienk "
"papier wat deur die Bemarking Departement vereis word vir 'n presiese taak, "
"beskikbaar en gelaai is binne-in die papier skinkborde).</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie afbakening:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o taak-hou-totdat=...      # voorbeeld: \"onbepaald\" of \"nie-hou\"  "
"</pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:87
msgid ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Page Labels</b></p>  "
"<p>Page Labels are printed by CUPS at the top and bottom of each page. They "
"appear on the pages surrounded by a little frame box. "
"<p>They contain any string you type into the line edit field.</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o page-label=\"...\"      # example: \"Company Confidential\"  </pre> "
"</p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Bladsy Etikette</b></p>  "
"<p>Bladsy Etikette is gedruk deur CUPS by die bo- en onderkant van elke bladsy. "
"Hulle verskyn op die bladsye omring deur klein raam boks. "
"<p>Hulle bevat enige string wat jy  binne-in die lyn redigeer veld tik.</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b>Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o bladsy-etiket=\"...\"      # voorbeeld: \"Maatskappy Vertroulik\"  "
"</pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kpschedulepage.cpp:102
msgid ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Job Priority</b></p>  "
"<p>Usually CUPS prints all jobs per queue according to the \"FIFO\" principle: "
"<em>First In, First Out</em>. "
"<p> The job priority option allows you to re-order the queue according to your "
"needs. "
"<p> It works in both directions: you can increase as well as decrease "
"priorities. (Usually you can only control your <b>own</b> jobs). "
"<p> Since the default job priority is \"50\", any job sent with, for example, "
"\"49\" will be printed only after all those others have finished. Conversely, a "
"\"51\" or higher priority job will go right to the top of a populated queue (if "
"no other, higher prioritized one is present).</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o job-priority=...   # example: \"10\" or \"66\" or \"99\"  </pre> "
"</p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt> "
"<p><b>Taak Voorrang</b></p>  "
"<p>Gewoonlik CUPS druk alle take per ry volgens die \"EIEU\" beginsel: <em>"
"Eeerste In, Eerste Uit</em>. "
"<p>Die taak voorrang opsie laat jou toe om die ry te herrangskik volgens jou "
"behoeftes. "
"<p>Dit werk in beide rigtings: jy kan prioriteite verhoog asook verlaag. "
"(Gewoonlik kan jy slegs jou <b>eie</b> take beheer). "
"<p>Aangesien die verstek taak voorrang \"50\" is, sal enige werk wat gestuur is "
"met, byvoorbeeld, \"49\" gedruk word slegs nadat al daardie ander klaar is. "
"Omgekeerd, 'n \"51\" of hoër voorrang werk sal reguit na die bokant van die "
"gepopuleerde ry gaan (indien geen ander, hoër prioriteit een teenwoordig is "
"nie).</p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o taak-prioriteit=...   # voorbeeld: \"10\" of \"66\" of \"99\"  "
"</pre> </p>  </qt>"

