#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:41
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Characters Per Inch</b></p>  "
"<p>This setting controls the horizontal size of characters when printing a text "
"file. </p> "
"<p>The default value is 10, meaning that the font is scaled in a way that 10 "
"characters  per inch will be printed. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o cpi=...          # example: \"8\" or \"12\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Karakters Per Duim</b></p>  "
"<p>Hierdie verstelling kontroleer die horisontale grootte van karakters wanneer "
"'n teks lêer gedruk word. </p> "
"<p>Die verstek waarde is 10, wat beteken dat die skriftipe is geskaal is in so "
"wyse dat 10 karakters per duim gedruk sal word. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie  parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o cpi=...          # voorbeeld: \"8\" of \"12\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:55
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Lines Per Inch</b></p>  "
"<p>This setting controls the vertical size of characters when printing a text "
"file. </p> "
"<p>The default value is 6, meaning that the font is scaled in a way that 6 "
"lines  per inch will be printed. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o lpi=...         # example \"5\" or \"7\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
"<qt>  "
"<p><b>Lyne Per Duim</b></p>  "
"<p>Hierdie verstelling kontroleer die vertikale grootte van karakters wanneer "
"'n teks lêer gedruk word. </p> "
"<p>Die verstek waarde is 6, wat beteken dat die skriftipe is  geskaal in 'n "
"wyse dat 6 lyne per duim gedruk sal word. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdrag kyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o lpi=...         # voorbeeld \"5\" of \"7\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:69
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Columns</b></p>  "
"<p>This setting controls how many columns of text will be printed on each page "
"when. printing text files. </p>  "
"<p>The default value is 1, meaning that only one column of text per page  will "
"be printed. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o columns=...     # example: \"2\" or \"4\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Kolomme</b></p>  "
"<p>Hierdie stel kontroleer hoeveel kolomme teks sal gedruk word op elke bladsy "
"wanneer teks lêers gedruk word. </p> "
"<p>Die verstek waarde is 1, wat beteken dat slegs een kolom teks per bladsy "
"gedruk sal word. </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o kolomme=...     # voorbeeld: \"2\" of \"4\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:84
msgid " <qt>  Preview icon changes when you turn on or off prettyprint.  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  Voorskou ikoon verander wanneer jy mooidruk aan of af skakel.  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:87
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Text Formats</b></p>  "
"<p>These settings control the appearance of text on printouts. They are only "
"valid for  printing text files or input directly through kprinter. </p>  "
"<p><b>Note:</b> These settings have no effect whatsoever for other input "
"formats than  text, or for printing from applications such as the KDE Advanced "
"Text Editor. (Applications  in general send PostScript to the print system, and "
"'kate' in particular has its own  knobs to control the print output. </p>. "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o cpi=...         # example: \"8\" or \"12\"  "
"<br>     -o lpi=...         # example: \"5\" or \"7\"  "
"<br>     -o columns=...     # example: \"2\" or \"4\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Teks formate</b></p>  "
"<p>Hierdie instellings beheer die voorkoms van teks op uitdrukke. Hulle is "
"slegs geldig vir die druk van teks lêers of toevoer direk deur kdrukker. </p>  "
"<p><b>Note:</b>Nota:</b> Hierdie instellings het geen effek hoegenaamd vir "
"ander toevoer formate anders as teks nie, of vir die druk vanaf toepassings "
"soos dieKDE Gevorderde Teks Redigeerder. (Toepassings in die algemeen stuur "
"Naskrif na die druk stelsel, en kate in besonder het sy eie knoppe om die druk "
"uitset te beheer. </p>. "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o cpi=...         # voorbeeld: \"8\" of \"12\"  "
"<br>     -o lpi=...         # voorbeeld: \"5\" or \"7\"  "
"<br>     -o kolomme=...     # voorbeeld: \"2\" of \"4\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:108
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Margins</b></p>  "
"<p>These settings control the margins of printouts on the paper. They are not "
"valid for  jobs originating from applications which define their own page "
"layout internally and  send PostScript to KDEPrint (such as KOffice or "
"OpenOffice.org). </p>  "
"<p>When printing from KDE applications, such as KMail and Konqueror, or "
"printing an ASCII text  file through kprinter, you can choose your preferred "
"margin settings here. </p>  "
"<p>Margins may be set individually for each edge of the paper. The combo box at "
"the bottom lets you change  the units of measurement between Pixels, "
"Millimeters, Centimeters, and Inches. </p>  "
"<p>You can even use the mouse to grab one margin and drag it to the intended "
"position (see the  preview picture on the right side). </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o page-top=...      # example: \"72\"  "
"<br>     -o page-bottom=...   # example: \"24\"  "
"<br>     -o page-left=...     # example: \"36\"  "
"<br>     -o page-right=...    # example: \"12\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Kantlyne</b></p>  "
"<p>Hierdie instellings beheer die kantlyne van uitdrukke op papier. Hulle is "
"nie geldig vir take wat ontstaan uit toepassings wat hul eie bladsy uitleg "
"intern bepaal en Naskrif stuur na KDEDruk (soos KOffice of OpenOffice. org) "
"nie. </p>  "
"<p>Wanneer gedruk word vanaf KDE toepassings, soos KMail en Konqueror, of  'n "
"ASCII teks lêer gedruk word deur kdrukker, kan jy jou voorrang kantlyn "
"instellings hier kies. </p>  "
"<p>Kantlyne mag individueel gestel wees vir elke kant van die papier. Die kombo "
"boks onder laat jou die eenhede van meting verander tussen Pixels, Millimeters, "
"Sentimeters, en Duime. </p>  "
"<p>Jy kan selfs die muis gebruik om een kantlyn te gryp en dit te trek tot by "
"die voorgenome posisie (sien die voorskou prent aan die regter kant). </p>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o bladsy bokant=...      # voorbeeld: \"72\"  "
"<br>     -o bladsy onderkant=...   # voorbeeld: \"24\"  "
"<br>     -o bladsy-links=...     # voorbeeld: \"36\"  "
"<br>     -o bladsy-regs=...    # voorbeeld: \"12\"  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:134
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Turn Text Printing with Syntax Highlighting (Prettyprint) On!</b></p>  "
"<p>ASCII text file printouts can be 'prettyfied' by enabling this option. If "
"you do so,  a header is printed at the top of each page. The header contains  "
"the page number, job title (usually the filename), and the date. In addition, C "
"and  C++ keywords are highlighted, and comment lines are italicized.</p> "
"<p>This prettyprint option is handled by CUPS.</p>  "
"<p>If you prefer another 'plaintext-to-prettyprint' converter, look for the <em>"
"enscript</em>  pre-filter on the <em>Filters</em> tab. </p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o prettyprint=true.  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Draai Teks Druk met Sintakses Verligting (Prettyprint) Aan!</b></p> "
"<p>ASCII teks lêer uitdrukke kan mooi gemaak word deur die aktivering van "
"hierdie opsie. Indien jy dit doen, word 'n bladsyhoof gedruk aan die bokant van "
"elke bladsy. Die bladsyhoof bevat die bladsynommer, taak titel (gewoonlik die "
"lêernaam), en die datum.  Bykomend, C en C++ sleutelwoorde word verlig, en "
"kommentaar lyne is gekursiveer.</> "
"<p>Hierdie prettyprint opsie is gehanteer deur CUPS.</p> "
"<p>Indien jy 'n ander eenvoudige teks -tot- prettyprint omkeerder verkies, kyk "
"vir die <em>enscript,/em>vooraf-filter op die <em>Filtreerders</em> "
"oortjie. </p> "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o prettyprint=waar.  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:153
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Turn Text Printing with Syntax Highlighting (Prettyprint) Off! </b></p>  "
"<p>ASCII text file printing with this option turned off are appearing without a "
"page  header and without syntax highlighting. (You can still set the page "
"margins, though.) </p>  "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o prettyprint=false  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Draai Teks Druk met Sintakses Verligting (Prettyprint) Af! </b></p>  "
"<p>ASCII teks lêer gedruk met hierdie opsie af, verskyn sonder 'n bladsyhoof en "
"sonder sintakses verligting. (Jy kan egter steeds die bladsy kantlyne stel. ) "
"</p>  "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>    -o prettyprint=onwaar  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

#: cups/kptextpage.cpp:167
msgid ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Print Text with Syntax Highlighting (Prettyprint)</b></p>  "
"<p>ASCII file printouts can be 'prettyfied' by enabling this option. If you do "
"so,  a header is printed at the top of each page. The header contains  the page "
"number, job title (usually the filename), and the date. In addition, C and  C++ "
"keywords are highlighted, and comment lines are italicized.</p> "
"<p>This prettyprint option is handled by CUPS.</p>  "
"<p>If you prefer another 'plaintext-to-prettyprint' converter, look for the <em>"
"enscript</em>  pre-filter on the <em>Filters</em> tab. </p>  "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Additional hint for power users:</b> This KDEPrint GUI element "
"matches  with the CUPS commandline job option parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o prettyprint=true.  "
"<br>     -o prettyprint=false  </pre> </p>  </qt>"
msgstr ""
" <qt>  "
"<p><b>Druk Teks met Sintakses Verligting (Prettyprint)</b></p>  "
"<p>ASCII lêer uitdrukke kan mooi gemaak word deur die aktivering van hierdie "
"opsie. Indien jy dit doen, word 'n bladsyhoof aan die bokant van elke bladsy "
"gedruk. Die bladsyhoof bevat die bladsynommer, taak titel (gewoonlik die "
"lêeraam), en die datum. Bykomend word C en C++ sleutelwoorde verlig, en "
"kommentaar lyne is gekursiveer. </p> "
"<p>Hierdie prettyprint opsie word hanteer deur CUPS.</p>  "
"<p>Indien jy 'n ander eenoudige teks -tot- prettyprint omkeerder verkies, kyk "
"vir die <em>enscript</em> vooraf-filtreerder op die <em>Filtreerders</em> "
"oortjie. </p>  "
"<br>  "
"<hr>  "
"<p><em><b>Addisionele wenk vir krag gebruikers:</b> Hierdie KDEDruk GUI element "
"stem ooreen met die CUPS opdraglyn taak opsie parameter:</em>  "
"<pre>     -o prettyprint=waar.  "
"<br>     -o prettyprint=onwaar  </pre> </p>  </qt>"

